=== Test: does E_PCP(q) and E_PCP(q)^(-1) ever share a non-trivial x? ===

If P ∈ E_PCP(q)(Q) with x_P = a, and there exists Q ∈ E_twist(Q) with x_Q = a, then:
  y_P^2 = a(a+1)(a+q^2)  and  y_Q^2 = a(a-1)(a-q^2)
  Product: y_P^2 y_Q^2 = a^2 (a^2-1)(a^2-q^4)
  So a^2(a^2-1)(a^2-q^4) is a square. Setting u = a^2:
  u (u-1)(u - q^4) is a square -- this is the GROSS / curve E*: v^2 = u(u-1)(u-q^4).

So PCP exists at fiber q ⟺ E*(q): v^2 = u(u-1)(u-q^4) has a rational point with u > 0, u ≠ 0, 1, q^4.

E*(q): y^2 = x(x-1)(x-q^4) — another elliptic curve in the family!
This is the 'product' / 'gluing' Kummer-like curve.

