=== This new curve E*(q): y^2 = x(x-1)(x-q^4) is the 'fusion curve'. ===
It captures EXACTLY the PCP intersection.

=== Geometric interpretation ===
E_PCP(q):    y_1^2 = x(x+1)(x+q^2)
E_twist(q):  y_2^2 = x(x-1)(x-q^2)  -- via twist by -1, X -> -X, Y -> i Y

Actually let me re-derive E_twist x-coords. Twist by d=-1 of [0,a2,0,a4,0]:
  E^(d): X^3 + a2 d X^2 + a4 d^2 X
  For E_PCP: [0, 1+q^2, 0, q^2, 0] in the (x, y) world.
  Twist by -1: [0, -(1+q^2), 0, q^2, 0] => y^2 = X^3 - (1+q^2)X^2 + q^2 X = X(X-1)(X-q^2).
  Yes, 2-torsion at X = 0, 1, q^2.

So if P_1 = (a, y_1) ∈ E_PCP(Q) and P_2 = (a, y_2) ∈ E_twist(Q) with SAME x = a:
  y_1^2 y_2^2 = a^2 (a^2 - 1)(a^2 - q^2)^2  ... wait no.
